/-! # Yap: matching a fix as `NSRegularExpression` does

A fix's pattern is `(?<![\w-])heard(?![\w-])`, case-insensitive (`DictationDictionary.apply`).
ICU, which runs it, compares the heard text and the transcript by full case folding: a span of
the transcript matches when its code points' foldings, joined, equal the heard text's (so `ß`
matches `ss`, `K` the Kelvin sign, `ﬀ` `ff`, but `f` not `ﬀ`). The two tables here were read from
the engine itself, for every code point (docs/yap-parity.md): `wordText`, where `[\w-]` starts
and stops matching, and `foldText`, every code point `u_strFoldCase` changes, with its folding. -/

@[expose] public section

namespace Examples.Yap.Fold

